From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LunaticKochiya <125438787@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] kernel: config-6.18: explicitly disable CONFIG_TCP_CONG_BBR1

The BBRv3 backport (hack-6.18/951-net-tcp-bbr3-support.patch) adds a new
TCP_CONG_BBR1 Kconfig symbol for the legacy BBRv1 module. Since
target/linux/generic/config-6.18 has no entry for it, the non-interactive
kernel configuration asks for a value and aborts the build:

  * Restart config...
  BBRv1 TCP (TCP_CONG_BBR1) [N/m/y/?] (NEW)
  make[8]: *** [scripts/kconfig/Makefile:85: syncconfig] Error 1

BBRv3 registers itself as "bbr" (CONFIG_TCP_CONG_BBR) and that is the
only module packaged by kmod-tcp-bbr, so disable the unused BBR1 module.

Signed-off-by: LunaticKochiya <125438787@qq.com>
---
diff --git a/target/linux/generic/config-6.18 b/target/linux/generic/config-6.18
--- a/target/linux/generic/config-6.18
+++ b/target/linux/generic/config-6.18
@@ -7106,6 +7106,7 @@
 # CONFIG_TCP_AO is not set
 CONFIG_TCP_CONG_ADVANCED=y
 # CONFIG_TCP_CONG_BBR is not set
+# CONFIG_TCP_CONG_BBR1 is not set
 # CONFIG_TCP_CONG_BIC is not set
 # CONFIG_TCP_CONG_CDG is not set
 CONFIG_TCP_CONG_CUBIC=y
-- 
2.43.0

